Could the above suspended groups also be detected by standard community detection algorithms? To address this question, we consider three community detection algorithms, i.e., the modularity maximization by the Leiden algorithm27, Infomap21, and the dcSBM25. We apply the algorithms and evaluate whether or not the detected communities match the suspended groups under the same matching criteria used for testing CIDRE. These community detection algorithms have found at least three times more groups than those found by CIDRE. However, none of them matches the suspended groups, with a small overlap of \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
